  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(499.088pt, 154.2pt, "IEEE")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(59.76pt, 191.997pt, "Abstract")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.837pt, 191.997pt, "—Conventional microwave heating techniques are ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 203.157pt, "limited due to inherent thermal point residency effects and ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 214.074pt, "inadequate control over the heating process. A novel method is ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 224.874pt, "proposed to enhance microwave heating uniformity using the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 235.791pt, "injection-pulling technique. In this method, the injection-pulling ")
  #line-at(46.791pt, 246.591pt, "technique is employed to achieve simultaneous modulation of ")
  #line-at(46.791pt, 257.508pt, "both the output phase and frequency of the magnetron, thereby ")
  #line-at(46.791pt, 268.308pt, "extending the locking bandwidth of the injection-locking ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 279.225pt, "technique. The output characteristics of the injection-pulled ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 290.025pt, "magnetron were validated through numerical calculations and ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 300.942pt, "experiments. Microwave heating experiments were conducted ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 311.859pt, "under both a five-cup water load and an absorbent paper load. ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 322.659pt, "Compared to conventional injection-locking frequency sweeping, ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 333.576pt, "the proposed method not only expands the sweeping bandwidth ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 344.376pt, "from 8 MHz to 18 MHz but also further improves heating ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 355.293pt, "uniformity, offering more options for magnetron applications in ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 366.093pt, "microwave heating. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(46.8pt, 388.44pt, "Index Terms")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(98.757pt, 388.44pt, "— injection-locking, injection-pulling technique, ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 398.763pt, "microwave heating uniformity, magnetron, phase-frequency ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 409.086pt, "simultaneous modulation ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(131.042pt, 443.876pt, "I.")
  #line-at(138.96pt, 443.88pt, "INTRODUCTION ")
  #line-at(92.636pt, 459.358pt, "ITH the advancement of electronic technology, ")
  #line-at(92.636pt, 471.479pt, "microwave heating has gained increasing attention ")
  #line-at(92.636pt, 483.6pt, "in industrial applications, such as food processing ")
  #line-at(46.78pt, 495.602pt, "and plastics manufacturing [1][2][3]. Magnetrons, which offer ")
  #line-at(46.79pt, 507.724pt, "the advantages of low cost, compact size, high output power, ")
  #line-at(46.79pt, 519.725pt, "and high efficiency, have become the predominant choice for ")
  #line-at(46.79pt, 531.847pt, "microwave heating in industrial applications [4][5]. However, ")
  #line-at(46.78pt, 543.968pt, "a magnetron demonstrates inherent limitations including ")
  #line-at(46.78pt, 555.97pt, "power output instability and poor phase noise characteristics ")
  #line-at(46.79pt, 568.091pt, "[6][7]. Consequently, microwave heating systems are ")
  #line-at(46.79pt, 580.212pt, "frequently prone to issues such as non-uniform heating, load ")
  #line-at(46.78pt, 592.214pt, "mismatch, and inadequate process controllability during ")
  #line-at(46.78pt, 604.336pt, "operational heating procedures [8][9]. ")
  #line-at(56.969pt, 616.337pt, "Extensive research has been conducted to solve the problem ")
  #line-at(46.77pt, 628.459pt, "of poor microwave heating uniformity [10][11]. The most ")
  #line-at(46.77pt, 640.58pt, "common method for improving the uniformity of microwave ")
  #line-at(46.77pt, 652.582pt, "heating is to use mode stirrers, which enhance uniformity by ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.88pt, 675.48pt, "This work was supported in part by the National Natural Science ")
  #line-at(46.798pt, 684.718pt, "Foundation of China under Grants U2015A22 and 60301004. ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 693.956pt, "X. Zhu, S. Wang, D. He, and C. Liu are with the School of Electronics and ")
  #line-at(46.798pt, 703.073pt, "Information Engineering, Sichuan University, Chengdu 610064, China ")
  #line-at(46.798pt, 712.311pt, "(")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#5b9bd5"))
  #line-at(49.435pt, 712.311pt, "Corresponding author:")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(126pt, 712.311pt, "Changjun Liu")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(170.276pt, 712.311pt, ". e-mail: cjliu@ieee.org). ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 721.549pt, "J. Hu is with the Shenzhen Technology Center of Guangdong Whirlpool ")
  #line-at(46.798pt, 730.667pt, "Electrical Appliances Co. Ltd., Shenzhen 518000, China ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(313.2pt, 192.36pt, "altering the electromagnetic field modes in the cavity ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 204.481pt, "[12][13][14][15]. Additionally, multi-frequency heating is ")
  #line-at(313.21pt, 216.603pt, "proposed to address the issues associated with single-")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 228.604pt, "frequency operation. Yang et al. proposed a frequency-")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 240.726pt, "complementary technique to enhance the uniformity of ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 252.847pt, "microwave heating [16]. Du et al. validated that multi-")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 264.849pt, "frequency excitation within 3.6-10 MHz frequency intervals ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 276.97pt, "could not only improve heating uniformity but also, to some ")
  #line-at(313.19pt, 288.972pt, "extent, enhance heating efficiency [17]. ")
  #line-at(323.399pt, 301.093pt, "The injection-locking technique is also a valid method for ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 313.215pt, "achieving variable-frequency heating, which provides precise ")
  #line-at(313.19pt, 325.217pt, "control of a magnetron operational frequency and phase ")
  #line-at(313.19pt, 337.338pt, "through the injection of an external signal with proximity to ")
  #line-at(313.19pt, 349.34pt, "the magnetron free-running frequency [18][19][20]. Yang et al. ")
  #line-at(313.19pt, 361.461pt, "implemented dynamic frequency sweeping with a 20-MHz ")
  #line-at(313.19pt, 373.582pt, "bandwidth during heating processing, which significantly ")
  #line-at(313.19pt, 385.584pt, "improved heating uniformity [21]. However, extant research ")
  #line-at(313.205pt, 397.681pt, "primarily focuses on the injection-locking state of a magnetron. ")
  #line-at(313.205pt, 409.803pt, "The spectrum outside the locking bandwidth is not effectively ")
  #line-at(313.195pt, 421.804pt, "utilized, which limits the selectable frequency range of the ")
  #line-at(313.195pt, 433.926pt, "sweep. ")
  #line-at(323.394pt, 445.928pt, "This paper proposes a novel method to enhance heating ")
  #line-at(313.195pt, 458.049pt, "uniformity by leveraging the injection-pulling state of the ")
  #line-at(313.185pt, 470.17pt, "magnetron. This methodology utilizes a single-sweep ")
  #line-at(313.185pt, 482.172pt, "frequency signal to achieve simultaneous modulation of both ")
  #line-at(313.185pt, 494.293pt, "the output phase and frequency of the magnetron. Microwave ")
  #line-at(313.185pt, 506.415pt, "heating experiments were conducted using various modulation ")
  #line-at(313.185pt, 518.416pt, "strategies, including sweep frequency within the injection-")
  #line-at(313.195pt, 530.538pt, "pulling range. The results demonstrate an improvement in ")
  #line-at(313.195pt, 542.539pt, "heating uniformity for the five-cup water load and absorbent ")
  #line-at(313.195pt, 554.661pt, "paper load. ")
