  #line-at(46.805pt, 424.809pt, "power spectrum and time-varying phase of the magnetron were ")
  #line-at(46.795pt, 436.811pt, "calculated, (1) and (2) were solved using the fourth-order ")
  #line-at(46.765pt, 448.932pt, "Runge-Kutta method, and the output spectrum was calculated ")
  #line-at(46.765pt, 461.053pt, "via the Fast Fourier Transformation (FFT). In the calculation, ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(46.765pt, 473.055pt, "Q")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(53.88pt, 474pt, "0")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(57pt, 473.04pt, " is set to 1200, and k is set to 0.002.  ")
  #line-at(57.01pt, 485.161pt, "Fig. 1(a) illustrates the calculated output spectrum of the ")
  #line-at(46.801pt, 497.283pt, "magnetron under injection-locking and injection-pulling states. ")
  #line-at(46.801pt, 509.284pt, "The injection-pulled magnetron's output spectrum introduces ")
  #line-at(46.801pt, 521.406pt, "additional frequency components compared to the injection-")
  #line-at(46.801pt, 533.408pt, "locking state. When the injected signal’s frequency just exceeds ")
  #line-at(46.791pt, 545.529pt, "the locking range, the frequency of the magnetron’s peak power ")
  #line-at(46.791pt, 557.65pt, "is still controlled by the injected signal, and this state is referred ")
  #line-at(46.791pt, 569.652pt, "to as peak-power pulling. As the frequency of the injected ")
  #line-at(46.781pt, 581.773pt, "signal continues to deviate, the amplitude of the magnetron’s ")
  #line-at(46.781pt, 593.775pt, "primary peak gradually diminishes. In contrast, the secondary ")
  #line-at(46.781pt, 605.896pt, "peak’s amplitude progressively grows, eventually evolving into ")
  #line-at(46.781pt, 618.018pt, "a state of equal-amplitude output. Therefore, based on the ")
  #line-at(46.781pt, 630.02pt, "characteristics of the injection-pulling state, if a sweep ")
  #line-at(46.781pt, 642.141pt, "frequency signal is introduced, the controllable range of its peak ")
  #line-at(46.781pt, 654.262pt, "power has been enhanced compared to conventional injection ")
  #line-at(46.781pt, 666.264pt, "locking. ")
  #line-at(56.98pt, 678.385pt, "Furthermore, as shown in Fig. 1(b), the injection-pulled ")
  #line-at(46.781pt, 690.387pt, "magnetron’s output phase contains a modulation component, ")
  #line-at(46.781pt, 702.508pt, "and ")
  #line-at(72.221pt, 702.508pt, "it ")
  #line-at(88.784pt, 702.508pt, "undergoes ")
  #line-at(140.265pt, 702.508pt, "periodic ")
  #line-at(183.465pt, 702.508pt, "temporal ")
  #line-at(229.426pt, 702.508pt, "variations. ")
  #line-at(281.384pt, 702.508pt, "This ")
  #line-at(46.781pt, 714.63pt, "phenomenon indicates that complex modulation of the ")
  #line-at(46.781pt, 726.632pt, "magnetron’s frequency and phase is incorporated into the output. ")
  #line-at(46.781pt, 738.753pt, "This time-varying frequency and phase result in rapid ")
  #line-at(313.171pt, 237.396pt, "fluctuations of the microwave modes within the heating cavity, ")
  #line-at(313.171pt, 249.518pt, "thereby enhancing the uniformity of heating. Microwave ")
  #line-at(313.171pt, 261.52pt, "heating experiments were conducted using this method to verify ")
  #line-at(313.171pt, 273.641pt, "the improvement in heating uniformity. ")
  #line-at(357.214pt, 297.644pt, "III.")
  #line-at(371.88pt, 297.6pt, "M")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(380.76pt, 297.6pt, "ICROWAVE ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(425.88pt, 297.6pt, "H")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(433.08pt, 297.6pt, "EATING ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(464.76pt, 297.6pt, "E")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(470.88pt, 297.6pt, "XPERIMENTS")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(313.205pt, 315.239pt, "A. Experimental Preparation ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(323.284pt, 329.641pt, "Under experimental conditions, the magnetron’s output ")
  #line-at(313.205pt, 341.763pt, "exhibits four distinct states as illustrated in Fig. 2: free-")
  #line-at(313.205pt, 353.764pt, "running, injection-locking, peak-power pulling, and equal-")
  #line-at(313.185pt, 365.886pt, "amplitude pulling states. At the peak-power pulling and equal-")
  #line-at(313.195pt, 378.007pt, "amplitude pulling states, their spectra are shown in Fig. 2(c) ")
  #line-at(313.205pt, 390.009pt, "and (d) with the injection locking frequency lower than the ")
  #line-at(313.205pt, 402.13pt, "locking band. Similar spectra will appear when the injection ")
  #line-at(313.205pt, 414.132pt, "locking frequency is higher than the locking band. The ")
  #line-at(313.205pt, 426.253pt, "following modulation strategies have been formulated: Ⅰ. Free-")
  #line-at(313.195pt, 438.375pt, "running state; Ⅱ. Sweeping frequency within the injection-")
  #line-at(313.195pt, 451.094pt, "locking range (2.450 ")
  #line-at(417.476pt, 451.094pt, " 2.458 GHz); and Ⅲ. Sweeping ")
  #line-at(313.204pt, 463.215pt, "frequency within the injection-pulling and injection-locking ")
  #line-at(313.194pt, 475.336pt, "range (2.443- 2.461 GHz).  ")
  #line-at(323.274pt, 487.457pt, "An experimental system is established to verify the heating ")
  #line-at(313.194pt, 499.459pt, "performance of the injection-modulated magnetron. The diagram ")
  #line-at(313.184pt, 511.581pt, "of the magnetron experimental system used in this paper is shown ")
  #line-at(313.184pt, 523.702pt, "in Fig. 3(a). Fig. 3(b)")
  #line-at(406.191pt, 523.702pt, "shows a photograph of the system. The ")
  #line-at(313.194pt, 535.704pt, "magnetron (LG 2M22603GWH) in the experiment is powered by ")
  #line-at(313.194pt, 547.825pt, "a switch-mode power supply (WELAMP 2000F, Magmeet). The ")
  #line-at(313.194pt, 559.827pt, "output spectrum of the magnetron is measured by a spectrum ")
  #line-at(313.194pt, 571.948pt, "analyzer (FSV, R&S), and the output power is measured by a ")
  #line-at(313.194pt, 584.069pt, "power meter (AV2433, Ceyear). A signal generator (HMC-")
  #line-at(313.194pt, 596.071pt, "T2220, Hittite) and a power amplifier (ZHL-30W-262, Mini-")
  #line-at(313.185pt, 608.193pt, "Circuits) generate the injection signal. We utilize a host ")
  #line-at(313.194pt, 620.194pt, "computer to control the sweeping frequency of the signal ")
  #line-at(313.194pt, 632.316pt, "generator. We use two circulators to inject an external signal, ")
  #line-at(313.184pt, 644.437pt, "thereby protecting the power amplifier and signal generator. The ")
  #line-at(313.184pt, 656.439pt, "experimental procedure is as follows: ")
  #line-at(323.284pt, 668.52pt, "Five cups, each containing 100g ± 1g of pure water, are placed ")
  #line-at(313.201pt, 680.641pt, "on a thermally insulating pad, and the initial temperature is ")
  #line-at(313.201pt, 692.643pt, "measured using an UNI-T UT325F thermometer. The cups are ")
  #line-at(313.211pt, 704.764pt, "positioned in the cavity according to the configuration in Fig. ")
  #line-at(313.211pt, 716.766pt, "3(b), and heating is maintained for 95 seconds. After the heating ")
  #line-at(313.22pt, 728.888pt, "process, remove the cups and return them to the insulating pad. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(318pt, 194.76pt, "Fig. 2.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(346.44pt, 194.76pt, " Magnetron output spectra with (a) free-running, (b) ")
  #line-at(317.991pt, 205.677pt, "injection-locking, (c) peak-power pulling, and (d) equal-amplitude ")
  #line-at(318pt, 216.48pt, "pulling states.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.238pt, 162.962pt, "(a)")
  #line-at(108.236pt, 162.962pt, "                                        (b) ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(50.28pt, 174.24pt, "Fig. 1. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.551pt, 174.24pt, "The (a) spectrum and (b) time-varying phase of ")
  #line-at(50.271pt, 185.04pt, "magnetron under various states.")
