  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.541pt, 602.664pt, " are computed. The heating results under different loads ")
  #line-at(46.782pt, 614.188pt, "are shown in TABLE I.")
  #line-at(56.981pt, 625.712pt, "For both the five-cup water load and the absorbent paper ")
  #line-at(46.782pt, 637.833pt, "load, the heating uniformity results consistently show strategy ")
  #line-at(46.782pt, 649.835pt, "III > II > I. Compared to the free-running condition, the ")
  #line-at(46.772pt, 661.956pt, "heating uniformity of a five-cup water load improved by 9% ")
  #line-at(46.762pt, 673.958pt, "under strategy III. In contrast, the uniformity improvement for ")
  #line-at(46.752pt, 686.079pt, "the absorbent paper load was even more pronounced. ")
  #line-at(46.752pt, 698.201pt, "Furthermore, the improvement in hotspot distribution across ")
  #line-at(46.752pt, 710.202pt, "different strategy is more visually demonstrated in Fig. 4. ")
  #line-at(56.961pt, 722.324pt, "In the free-running state, the magnetron operates at a single ")
  #line-at(46.762pt, 734.326pt, "fixed frequency, resulting in the poorest heating uniformity. ")
  #line-at(313.162pt, 165.41pt, "Under conventional injection-locking frequency sweeping, the ")
  #line-at(313.152pt, 177.412pt, "magnetron output is precisely locked by an external signal ")
  #line-at(313.152pt, 189.534pt, "with phase coherence, featuring a narrow frequency sweep ")
  #line-at(313.152pt, 201.535pt, "range and relatively slow, orderly variations. After introducing ")
  #line-at(313.152pt, 213.657pt, "the injection-pulling state, the magnetron output exhibits ")
  #line-at(313.152pt, 225.778pt, "multiple-frequency components, intense phase jumps, strong ")
  #line-at(313.142pt, 237.78pt, "randomness, and a broader frequency sweep range, ultimately ")
  #line-at(313.142pt, 249.901pt, "resulting in improved heating uniformity. ")
  #line-at(323.331pt, 262.023pt, "TABLE II compares the proposed method with the ")
  #line-at(313.132pt, 274.024pt, "conventional injection-locking frequency sweeping method. It ")
  #line-at(313.132pt, 286.146pt, "is observed that under identical injection intensity, the ")
  #line-at(313.142pt, 298.148pt, "proposed method extends the frequency sweep bandwidth ")
  #line-at(313.142pt, 310.269pt, "from 8 MHz to 18 MHz, providing additional spectral range ")
  #line-at(313.142pt, 322.39pt, "for sweep strategies. Moreover, the experiments achieved ")
  #line-at(313.142pt, 334.392pt, "multi-frequency scanning output with phase randomness using ")
  #line-at(313.142pt, 346.513pt, "only a single external sweep frequency signal. ")
